From 310f0adec187284fecff3eea69faccef679a3c7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: coalesce outbound inventory with a short suppression
 window

Coalesce outbound transaction inventory for an average 25 ms, retaining the
shared randomized inbound timer at 50 ms. Incoming announcements can suppress
queued duplicates before the next send. Wire the millisecond constants into
net processing and retain bounded inventory bursts and recent-relay caching.
The historical rationale named different constants; this payload uses 2,500
for burst sizing and retains 350,000 recent announcements. It does not implement
a strict 2,500 items/second rate limiter.

Original-Commit: 23b0b69b1c0c517ba82d8baa46c723975eda5000
Original-Patch: ecash/011
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Complete the inventory timing owner with millisecond inbound scheduling and a 25 ms randomized outbound delay; retain exact suppression and constant assertions, use a nonzero test send buffer, and omit handler ownership and future batch APIs now assigned to their actual purpose owners.

Plan-v2 owner repair: C: separate normal and fast clocks and preserve local-origin/low-bandwidth trickle using only the early single-transaction relay API.

